WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.390 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  there's no denying that competitive  gaming is on the rise with tournaments  for league of legends overwatch and  Street Fighter 5 entertaining millions  of viewers and rewarding millions of  dollars each year so it comes as no  surprise that breakaway Amazon's first  game from their newly established game  development studio just so happens to be  a 4v4 competitive brawler while it does  fit the profile of a typical eSports  title the game's frantic gameplay and  well-designed heroes up a refreshing if  oddly familiar experience that longs to  hang with the likes of the after  mentioned competitive gaming giants now  a MOBA this game is not but you can feel  the essence of dota or League of Legends  coursing through breakaways veins two  teams of four heroes compete to grab the  relic in the center of the arena and  deliver to the enemy base fighting off  anyone that stands in the way  breakaway offers a selection of  mythological heroes to choose from eight  in the most current alpha build each  with their own unique set of abilities  while the character design isn't the  most creative or inspired they're  recognizable enough for you to at least  understand what their strengths might be  just by looking at them big guy tank gun  guy damage lady with headdress healer  while the characters aren't exactly  memorable enough to write home about the  gameplay seems to be a strong enough  pedestal to support their shortcomings  the inclusion of buildable z' is  something that helps set Breakaway apart  from other similar games being both  offensive and defensive they cause each  team's base to assume in almost  maze-like appearance with players  capable of adding up to eight structures  each subsequent round combine this with  an upgrade system that the game  encourages you to utilize between deaths  matches can wind up being an extremely  hectic and fast-paced affair after just  a couple of rounds  and this is where the game can get a  little messy matches where players have  built up their bases can result in a  whirlwind of attacks saturating the  screen parsing through all the mayhem  can reveal a surprising inner layer of  depth and complexity but breakaway seems  to favor the chaos leading to some  exciting and seemingly unfair outcomes  holding on to the relic for longer than  a couple seconds can sometimes feel like  an impossible task every single hit that  character takes will cause a relative  change hands and by the later rounds  enemy encounters begin to feel more like  hot potato than anything else but the  strategy is still there passing the  relic to another player while you stun  an enemy heading towards you and then  dashing past them to set up an alley-oop  with a relic it's a satisfying prospect  that breakaway dangles in front of us  like a carrot on a stick  granted the game is still early in  development and players will become more  skilled as time goes on but as it stands  right now breakaway offers a very  distinct level of joy one that feels  tantamount to any other online shooter  or MOBA out there breakaway is not a  game that will blow you away with its  innovative game player groundbreaking  mechanics but it's a game that where's  its influences on sleeve it doesn't  introduce many new ideas but the ones  that retreads  helped create a solid foundation for an  exciting new take on the genre  [Music]

